      {
        "id": 211508,
        "name": "sliceknot",
        "username": "sliceknot",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/4bbf92/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-12T00:45:23.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This ability seems very overpowered to me if it is unlimited. This means that in two rounds she can take out an entire horde of d6 minions single handedly because even if she rolls poorly and every minions saves, they will be reduced to d4s and then next time will be destroyed. I like the idea of zones, but there is no mention of this in the rules. Do I, as GM, set each group of three minions as being in a single zone? The problem I have with this is that I feel in story terms, Tachyon should be able to attack the entire horde of minions in one round regardless of how seperated they are, but maybe that if she does the attack shouldn't be enough to destroy them so quickly.&nbsp;<span>To contrast this to the card game, the card hypersonic assault does 1 damage to each non-hero (villian?) target which is something, but not much at all.</span></p><p>I am currious how other people feel about this. Is this not a problem because minions are meant to be this weak? Or am I missing a more simple way to nerf this ability?</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:42:04.973Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
