        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rickjonzz/{size}/1934_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-01-12T15:10:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"sliceknot\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/4bbf92/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> sliceknot:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Is this not a problem because minions are meant to be this weak? Or am I missing a more simple way to nerf this ability?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I ran 801 and 802 for my gaming group on Tuesday, and yeah, Tach sweeps minions off the board like they were paper. And if Legacy Galvanizes Tach, the minions might as well not show up. Galvanized Tach was regularly throwing 6 and up against d6 minions. I think that's part of the reason why they blew through the issues so fast.&nbsp;</p>",
